          {
            "title": "Naming",
            "id": 88828,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Similar to naming variables and functions, there are some common practices when defining classes.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Person\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, name, age)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.name = name\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.age = age\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"teacher = Person(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Emily&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"24\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"12\" /><option startIndex=\"98\" endIndex=\"104\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>Person</code>, followed by <code>Person</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You follow common naming practices for classes, just as you do for variables and functions.</p><p>Define the class <code>Person</code>, then create a teacher from it.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Person\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, name, age)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.name = name\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.age = age\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"teacher = Person(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Emily&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"24\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"12\" /><option startIndex=\"98\" endIndex=\"104\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"def\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"self\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>class</code>, followed by <code>Person</code>, and finally <code>Person</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Class name",
            "id": 89046,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Class names usually have the first letter capitalized and the rest lowercase, like with <code>Person</code> here.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Person\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, name, age)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.name = name\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.age = age\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"12\" /></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>Person</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Descriptive",
            "id": 88823,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Like variables, we try to name classes descriptively.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Book\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, author, title)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.author = author\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.title = title\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"B\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>class</code>, followed by <code>Book</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You choose descriptive class names, just as you do for variables.</p><p>Begin a class named <code>Book</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Book\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, author, title)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.author = author\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.title = title\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"10\" endIndex=\"11\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"def\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"author\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>class</code>, followed by <code>Book</code>, and finally <code>:</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Consistent",
            "id": 89048,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>As with naming variables and functions, we should name things consistently and watch out for capitalization.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Person\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, name, age)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.name = name\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.age = age\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"sayHello\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Hello&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"sayBye\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Bye&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"teacher = Person(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Emily&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"24\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"teacher.sayBye()\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"206\" endIndex=\"212\" /><option startIndex=\"212\" endIndex=\"213\" /><option startIndex=\"213\" endIndex=\"214\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"Saybye\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Bye\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>sayBye</code>, followed by <code>(</code>, and finally <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You name classes and methods consistently and watch their capitalization, just as with variables and functions.</p><p>Make the code print <code>Bye</code> by calling the right method on <code>teacher</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Person\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, name, age)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.name = name\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.age = age\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"sayHello\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Hello&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"sayBye\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Bye&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"teacher = Person(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Emily&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"24\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"teacher.sayBye()\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"198\" endIndex=\"205\" /><option startIndex=\"206\" endIndex=\"212\" /><option startIndex=\"212\" endIndex=\"213\" /><option startIndex=\"213\" endIndex=\"214\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"Person\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"sayHello\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Bye\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>teacher</code>, followed by <code>sayBye</code>, <code>(</code>, and finally <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Other features",
            "id": 88771,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Like methods outside of classes, you can use Python's built-in functions and core features.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Pie\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, flavor, ingredients)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.flavor = flavor\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.ingredients = ingredients\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"print_ingredients\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i \" /><text value=\"in\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" self.ingredients:    \" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"      print(i)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"applePie = Pie(\" /><text value=\"'apple'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", [\" /><text value=\"'flour'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"'eggs'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"'apples'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"'butter'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"applePie.print_ingredients()\" /><text type=\"break\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"150\" endIndex=\"153\" /><option startIndex=\"154\" endIndex=\"155\" /><option startIndex=\"156\" endIndex=\"158\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"flour\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"eggs\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"apples\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"butter\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>for</code>, followed by <code>i</code>, and finally <code>in</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Like methods outside of classes, you can use Python's built-in functions and core features.</p><p>Inside a method, an instance reaches its own data through <code>self</code>.</p><p>Loop over the pie's ingredients so the code prints each one.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Pie\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, flavor, ingredients)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.flavor = flavor\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.ingredients = ingredients\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"print_ingredients\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i \" /><text value=\"in\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" self.ingredients:    \" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"      print(i)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"applePie = Pie(\" /><text value=\"'apple'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", [\" /><text value=\"'flour'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"'eggs'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"'apples'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"'butter'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"applePie.print_ingredients()\" /><text type=\"break\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"121\" endIndex=\"138\" /><option startIndex=\"150\" endIndex=\"153\" /><option startIndex=\"159\" endIndex=\"175\" /><option startIndex=\"187\" endIndex=\"192\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"display_ingredients\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"while\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"self.flavor\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"return\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"flour\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"eggs\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"apples\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"butter\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>print_ingredients</code>, followed by <code>for</code>, <code>self.ingredients</code>, and finally <code>print</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 1",
            "id": 88796,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's wrong with this code?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"Person():\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, age, height)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  self.age = age\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  self.height = height\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"jess = Person(\" /><text value=\"29\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(jess.age)\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The <code>class</code> keyword is missing</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">There's nothing wrong with this code</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The <code>class</code> keyword is missing.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A class definition starts with the <code>class</code> keyword, followed by its name and a colon.</p><p>The first line is <code>Person():</code>. What must be fixed before the code can define <code>Person</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"Person():\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, age, height)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  self.age = age\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  self.height = height\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"jess = Person(\" /><text value=\"29\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(jess.age)\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Add the missing <code>class</code> keyword and use a class header</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Nothing, because parentheses alone define a class</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Pass <code>self</code> when calling <code>Person(29, 5)</code></item><item value=\"4\" correct=\"false\">Move <code>print(jess.age)</code> inside the class definition</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Add the missing <code>class</code> keyword and use a class header.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 2",
            "id": 88794,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How many values can we call the <code>Person</code> constructor with, without changing the given class?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Person\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, age, height)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  self.age = age\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  self.height = height\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"jess = Person(\" /><text value=\"29\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(jess.age)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"29\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">2</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">3</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick 2.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Python supplies <code>self</code> automatically when you create an instance.</p><p>If you change the call to <code>Person(29)</code>, why will it fail?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Person\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, age, height)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  self.age = age\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  self.height = height\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"jess = Person(\" /><text value=\"29\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(jess.age)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"29\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">It supplies age but leaves height without a value</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">It supplies self but leaves age and height without values</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">It supplies height but leaves age without a value</item><item value=\"4\" correct=\"false\">It needs a value for Person before age and height</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It supplies age but leaves height without a value.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 3",
            "id": 88795,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What Python core language features can we use inside a class?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">All of Python's core language features</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">We're just able to create variables</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">All of Python's core language features.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can use all of Python's core language features inside a class.</p><p>A class method needs a loop and an <code>if</code> statement to process a list. Is that design allowed?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Yes, methods can use those core Python features</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">No, a class can contain variables but no control flow</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">No, loops are allowed only outside class definitions</item><item value=\"4\" correct=\"false\">Yes, but only if the loop and condition are written outside the method</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Yes, methods can use those core Python features.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 4",
            "id": 88792,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which of these is not a good naming practice for classes?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Naming your classes with reserved language keywords like <code>if</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Capitalizing the first letter of a class name</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Naming your classes with reserved language keywords like <code>if</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Class names commonly start with a capital letter, and reserved Python keywords cannot be used as names.</p><p>A developer proposes naming a class <code>if</code>. Why should that name be rejected?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>if</code> is a reserved language keyword</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Every class name must contain an underscore</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Python allows only built-in type names for classes</item><item value=\"4\" correct=\"false\">Lowercase class names are always syntax errors, even when they are not keywords</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>if</code> is a reserved language keyword.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example 1",
            "id": 89488,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create a class that represents different book series, for example, Harry Potter, The Hunger Games, etc.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"BookSeries\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, name, books)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.name = name\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.books = books\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"book series\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"16\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>class</code>, followed by <code>BookSeries</code>, and finally <code>:</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create a class that represents different book series, for example, Harry Potter, The Hunger Games, etc.</p><p>Write the header for a class named <code>BookSeries</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"BookSeries\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, name, books)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.name = name\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.books = books\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"16\" /><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"def\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"books\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>class</code>, followed by <code>BookSeries</code>, and finally <code>:</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example 2",
            "id": 89489,
